meta {
  name: Create org API key
  type: http
  seq: 43
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/orgs/:id/api-keys
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  id: 
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "HR onboarding",
    "scopes": [
      "org:read",
      "members:write"
    ],
    "expires_in_days": 365,
    "ip_allowlist": [
      "203.0.113.0/24"
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  See docs/org-api.md §1. Requires the `orgs` and `org_api` feature flags. Owner or admin with a recent strong sign-in (`step_up_required` with `acr_values` and `max_age`; `403 step_up_unavailable` when the server has no strong-auth `acr` configured). `send_as` is required with `messages:send` and must be an active org agent. The secret is returned once (`Cache-Control: no-store`) and stored only as SHA-256. At most 25 live keys per org. A person signed in (member token); automation gets `human_required`.
}
